  "judgment": {
    "prospect_pts": 7,
    "prospect_why": "The case is that grid and utility capex pulls a small, underfollowed hardware maker along with it; the driver is already in the last print, revenue $212.7M vs $193M and EPS $4.49 vs $2.41 with gross margin up 29.7% to 34.3% over four quarters, so this is reported rather than guided or story.",
    "competition_pts": 6,
    "competition_why": "Gross margin widening while revenue grows is the cleanest moat evidence in the set; the nearest listed peer HUBB trades at 21.2x forward and the second, MacLean Power, is private so share data is unavailable, which is why this is 6 and not 7.",
    "macro_fit_pts": 5,
    "macro_fit_why": "Cash-generative industrial with 0.80x cash conversion fits a plateau regime and value leadership, but it is a small cap and small caps trailed large over the last month with a hike live for 16 September; XLI is up only 0.63% over three months.",
    "narrative_pts": 5,
    "narrative_why": "The case is grid buildout adjacency to the AI-power theme, but no account in the corpus mentions it and it is not a named theme stock, so it moves on its own numbers, which is safer and slower."
